title: Caravan Orchestrator anchor
---
[root] Caravan Orchestrator vertical slice (complete)
Remap the completed Caravan anchor onto a developer-authored Stage and Orchestrator without changing the immutable engine semantics. Build one small working slice in ordinary Rust, then use its traces to learn which orchestration patterns are worth extracting later.
Files: orchestrator.vine; proposals/caravan-orchestrator-anchor.md; spec/initial.md; spec/cellular-automata-anchor.md; spec/discontinuity-projection.md; proposals/stage-layer.md; proposals/input-and-interaction.md; crates/caravan-demo/**
Do: Dispatch the stages only after their dependencies are reviewed. Keep each packet's file ownership disjoint, keep the Orchestrator as mutable control code rather than authoritative game state, and preserve the three immutable seams.
Accept: A concrete Caravan Orchestrator can interpret one input packet set, produce one closed transformation, publish an immutable journal/worldline update, query arbitrary times, select a branch, and present a deterministic frame while all existing anchor evidence remains green.
-> anchor
-> demo-wiring
-> input-model
-> journal-publication
-> orchestrator-contract
-> orchestrator-core
-> orchestrator-evidence
-> stage-composition
-> transformation-model
> The engine's authoritative state changes only through publication of a new immutable journal/worldline value.
> The Orchestrator is ordinary developer-written imperative control code; no universal engine Orchestrator trait or loop API is introduced in this slice.
> Worldline, Journal, and GameState remain immutable published values; the Orchestrator may replace selected values but may not own an imperative board, actor layer, resource counter, effect layer, or current GameState.
> InteractionDefinition is the current pure seam: InputPacketSet + Tau + LogicalTime -> Transformation.
> Journal heterogeneity uses one closed game-owned enum/DU payload type; no runtime object collection, Any, or untyped journal bag.
> JournalWriter is the game-facing timestamp authority. No InputTime or packet timestamp is added.
> Camera, HUD, backend, device, host clock, and reusable DSL extraction are outside this slice.
---
ref [anchor] Completed indexed anchor (build.vine)
The completed anchor supplies ReferenceWorldline, JournalWriter, immutable branches, direct state queries, Playback, presentation, persistence, and the existing evidence required by this slice.
